messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: contrib/pds/tif_imageiter.c
Line: 349
Function: gtTileSeparate
Bug type: integer-overflow-to-heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: Buffer for 4 planar components is allocated with _TIFFmalloc(4 * tilesize) without checking for multiplication overflow. If tilesize is large enough, 4*tilesize overflows size_t, resulting in an under-sized allocation. Subsequent uses (e.g., memset(a, 0xff, tilesize) at line 360 and TIFFReadTile writes into r/g/b/a) will write tilesize bytes per plane past the end of the allocated heap buffer, causing a heap buffer overflow.

Source context:
